# CapitalOS environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the repo root, then run `make build && make up`.
#
# Nothing in this file is required to get the app running: docker-compose
# already provides working defaults for the database and auth secret, so
# `make up` boots cleanly with zero configuration. Everything below is for
# OPTIONAL third-party integrations (market data, crypto). Any feature whose
# key you skip will simply return a clear error when you try to use it —
# the rest of the app (dashboard, portfolio, accounts, cash flow, demo user
# login) works fully without any of this.

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Already defaulted in docker-compose.yml to match the bundled postgres
# service (postgresql://capitalos:capitalos@postgres:5432/capitalos).
# Only set this if you're pointing at a different Postgres instance.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://capitalos:capitalos@postgres:5432/capitalos

# ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Falls back to a shared, insecure development secret if unset — fine for
# local use, but set a real random value before exposing this beyond your
# own machine (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=

# AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN_ALG=HS256
# AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES=15
# AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL_DAYS=30
# AUTH_REFRESH_COOKIE_NAME=capitalos_refresh

# ── CORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed origins. Defaults to localhost:5173/4173
# (the Vite dev server / preview ports) if unset.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# ── Stock / market data providers ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Price refresh works with none of these set — Yahoo/yfinance is the default
# fallback for every exchange — but treat that as a last resort, not
# something to rely on for volume: it's an unofficial, undocumented endpoint
# and rate-limits aggressively and unpredictably (verified directly: even a
# single request can get a 429 after enough prior traffic, independent of
# batch size). FINNHUB_API_KEY is tried first for US symbols and is a real,
# documented API — recommended if you hold more than a couple of US
# positions (tested: fixed 24/24 previously-stale US symbols in one run).
# See docs/setup/api-keys.md for full details and signup links.
# FINNHUB_API_KEY=
# EODHD_API_KEY= # alternate provider, not in the default chain, but tested and works

# ── Crypto providers (all optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Price lookups already work with none of these set (free public APIs).
# Wallet holdings/balance sync is all-or-nothing per chain and DOES need a
# key. HELIUS_API_KEY for Solana holdings sync specifically (basic Solana
# RPC calls already fall back to a free public endpoint).
# See docs/setup/api-keys.md for full details and signup links.
# MORALIS_API_KEY= # recommended for EVM chains — also returns per-token USD prices
# ALCHEMY_API_KEY= # alternative to Moralis for EVM chains; either one alone is enough
# HELIUS_API_KEY=
# COINGECKO_API_KEY=
# HELIUS_RPC_URL=
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=
# Default: ethereum,base,arbitrum,optimism,mantle,scroll. Narrow this if you
# only hold on some EVM chains — fewer chains means fewer API calls per sync.
# CRYPTO_EVM_CHAINS=

# Coinbase (optional, for the daily Coinbase-account sync job). Generate a
# view-only Advanced Trade API key from the Coinbase Developer Platform.
# COINBASE_USERNAME= # must match your CapitalOS username
# COINBASE_KEY_ID= # e.g. organizations/{org_id}/apiKeys/{key_id}
# COINBASE_KEY_SECRET= # the EC private key PEM, with \n-escaped newlines on one line

# ── IBKR Flex Web Service (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, IBKR statement auto-sync is unavailable — manual CSV/XLS
# upload via the Ingest page still works. These come from your own IBKR
# account (Client Portal → Flex Queries / Flex Web Service), not a
# third-party site — see docs/setup/api-keys.md for the exact setup steps.
# This is ONE global set of credentials for ONE real IBKR account, shared by
# every user in this deployment (there's no per-user IBKR key). If you set
# these, you MUST also set IBKR_FLEX_USERNAME (or IBKR_FLEX_USER_ID) below —
# without it, sync refuses to run for anyone, on purpose: otherwise any user
# in the app (including the demo account) could trigger a pull of your real
# statement into their own records.
# IBKR_FLEX_TOKEN=
# IBKR_FLEX_QUERY_ID=
# IBKR_FLEX_USERNAME= # must match an existing CapitalOS username exactly

# ── Misc ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All of these are already read from the environment with the shown value
# as the code's built-in default (os.getenv(NAME, default) — not hardcoded
# in a way that ignores this file). Uncommenting with a different value is
# a real, meaningful change; uncommenting with the same value is a no-op.
SNAPSHOT_DAY=1
# TZ=UTC
# UPLOAD_STALE_DAYS=30
